{%- comment -%}
  US delivery nudge (5 Nov 2026) — nudges US visitors towards free delivery.

  How US delivery is charged (General profile, US zone, set in Shopify admin):
    • £25 flat per order (US customers see $35), however many bottles
    • free when the whisky in the order reaches £150
  Shopify sets that threshold in pounds, so the dollar line moves with the exchange
  rate: about $202 at 1.35 (Nov 2026). WB_FREE_CENTS below is rounded UP to $210 so
  everything we say stays true up to a rate of 1.40. If the £150 threshold changes
  in admin, change WB_FREE_CENTS here (threshold × today's rate, rounded up with
  ~4% headroom).

  Only Printful merch is exempt (its own profile ships free everywhere), so it's
  left out of the cart sum. The gift voucher needs no shipping.

  Only prints for a US visitor buying in USD — the $ figure is hard-coded. Outputs
  nothing otherwise, so callers keep their existing wording.

  Accepts:
    context — 'product' (wb-trust-strip delivery line; needs `product`)
              'cart'    (cart drawer + cart page tax note)

  Not verified: whether a discount code entered at checkout can take an order back
  under £150. The cart copy only ever reflects the cart total.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign WB_FREE_CENTS = 21000
  assign WB_FREE_TEXT = '$210'

  assign wb_us = false
  if localization.country.iso_code == 'US' and cart.currency.iso_code == 'USD'
    assign wb_us = true
  endif

  if wb_us and context == 'product' and product != blank and product.vendor != 'Printful'
    # price_min, not the selected variant: the line is server-rendered and doesn't
    # update on variant change, so it must be true for every variant.
    assign wb_two = product.price_min | times: 2
    if product.price_min >= WB_FREE_CENTS
      echo '<strong>Free US delivery</strong> — duties &amp; taxes included'
    elsif wb_two >= WB_FREE_CENTS
      echo '<strong>Order two and delivery’s free</strong> — one for them, one for you'
    else
      echo '<strong>Free US delivery over ' | append: WB_FREE_TEXT | append: '</strong> — duties &amp; taxes included'
    endif
  endif

  if wb_us and context == 'cart'
    assign wb_sub = 0
    assign wb_qty = 0
    for item in cart.items
      if item.requires_shipping and item.vendor != 'Printful'
        assign wb_sub = wb_sub | plus: item.final_line_price
        assign wb_qty = wb_qty | plus: item.quantity
      endif
    endfor

    if wb_qty > 0
      assign wb_two = wb_sub | times: 2
      if wb_sub >= WB_FREE_CENTS
        echo '<strong>Your order ships free to the US.</strong> Duties &amp; taxes included.'
      elsif wb_qty == 1 and wb_two >= WB_FREE_CENTS
        echo '<strong>Add a second bottle and US delivery is free.</strong> Duties &amp; taxes included.'
      else
        # Round the gap UP to whole dollars, so "$38 away" is never a cent short.
        assign wb_gap = WB_FREE_CENTS | minus: wb_sub | divided_by: 100.0 | ceil | times: 100
        capture wb_gap_text
          render 'wb-money', amount: wb_gap, code: false
        endcapture
        echo '<strong>You’re ' | append: wb_gap_text | append: ' away from free US delivery.</strong> Duties &amp; taxes included.'
      endif
    endif
  endif
-%}
